\title{Antichain, Sperner family}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Our first proof of Sperner’s Theorem, to be stated below, will be based on \ref{CC0A}. We shall freely interchange #{X} and #{[n]}, and write #{\mathcal{P}(n)} for #{\mathcal{P}(X) = \mathcal{P}([n])}. We call a family #{\mathcal{A} \subset \mathcal{P}(n)} an \em{antichain} or a \em{Sperner family} if no set in #{\mathcal{A}} is contained in another.}
